WEBVTT

chocolate-caption-1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.667
The recipe can stay

chocolate-caption-2
00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.467
the same.

chocolate-caption-3
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.500
The chocolate

chocolate-caption-4
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.867
doesn’t have to.

chocolate-caption-5
00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.100
Chocolate contains

chocolate-caption-6
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.067
cocoa butter,

chocolate-caption-7
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.467
a fat that forms crystals.

chocolate-caption-8
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:10.900
Melt it enough,

chocolate-caption-9
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.467
and that crystal structure

chocolate-caption-10
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:13.267
breaks down.

chocolate-caption-11
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.933
As it cools,

chocolate-caption-12
00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:16.267
crystals form again.

chocolate-caption-13
00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:17.600
But their arrangements,

chocolate-caption-14
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.533
and the network they build,

chocolate-caption-15
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:20.300
can differ.

chocolate-caption-16
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.500
The result can be

chocolate-caption-17
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.200
softer chocolate

chocolate-caption-18
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.267
with less snap.

chocolate-caption-19
00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:25.600
Tempering guides

chocolate-caption-20
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.633
that rebuilding

chocolate-caption-21
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.200
with controlled temperatures

chocolate-caption-22
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.267
and mixing.

chocolate-caption-23
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:31.567
The goal is a structure

chocolate-caption-24
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.700
that helps chocolate

chocolate-caption-25
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.433
snap cleanly

chocolate-caption-26
00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.533
and look glossy.

chocolate-caption-27
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.833
Same recipe.

chocolate-caption-28
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.733
Different structure.
